at apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$\n- **III.** $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186383687 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a540711c-ecf6-55f0-99c0-da5fdfa24e62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383687 #edb/ref 1074 "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be ${∅}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{a},{∅},{a,∅}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${∅}$ is ${∅,{∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1071 "If $X=\\{2,4,8\\}$, then $P(X)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "350a2acf-787e-5ee2-949f-2438ca3d2b8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395714 #edb/ref 1074 "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](images/58/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{2\\},\\,\\{4\\},\\,\\{8\\},\\,\\{2,4\\},\\,\\{2,8\\},\\,\\{4,8\\},\\,\\{2,4,8\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)=\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395715 #